0.01 2026-11-16
     - initial App::AnteREPL release, with the anterepl executable
     - added scrolling screen editing, numbered source, RUN, LIST ranges,
       slow/pause controls, undo, local EDITOR support, dump, and peek
     - LOAD accepts ordinary Perl and numbered BASIC PERL files; SAVE
       preserves the loaded format and writes plain source to .pl files
     - added AUTO entry with a default increment of 5; AUTO OFF or Ctrl-C
       ends entry without losing stored lines
     - added environment inspection, literal SET/UNSET, EDIT ENV using
       VAR=value files, SAVE/LOAD/RELOAD, and startup environment RESET
     - completed built-in HELP, linked the user wiki, and added a Dist::Zilla
       configuration with an explicit list of files for the CPAN release
     - implemented the terminal integration checks in Perl using IO::Pty
     - added CLS to clear the display while retaining the stored program,
       live Perl workspace, environment, AUTO settings, and source undo
     - fixed Ctrl-C during LIST on Unix with Term::ReadKey installed
     - made AUTO entry quiet by default, with AUTO ECHO ON/OFF control;
       documented multiline immediate execution and shared subroutines
     - made Ctrl-D end AUTO without exiting, restricted the EVAL command
       to uppercase, and added Shift-Enter/Ctrl-N for inserting a newline
       into the current screen entry without submitting it
     - clarified that EVAL leaves AUTO active and function definitions are
       silent; tested session-only functions without storing their source
     - removed the experimental STORE command and pending EVAL source state
     - added FUNCTIONS to list defined workspace functions, including imports;
       documented redefinition warnings and one-time EVAL setup statements
